@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+Unlike print, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. It does support ``highlight``, which defaults to ``True`` and forces highlighting on even if the Console was created with highlighting disabled, and a basic ``style``. Output still goes through the usual Console buffer and render hooks.
+
+
